nts (no CRD/Kubernetes resource renames, no localization review beyond the changed label) are carried into the epic's scope section and the fourth AC. The strategy has no open questions, risks, or prerequisites (no Documentation Support gate requiring a docs-authoring epic), so nothing was silently dropped.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9700e729b2052218","agent_id":"a0ea5c6f2a391851c","session_id":"88ce6bf4-875c-4392-8973-978cd309636c","uuid":"9b849452-b476-4151-b6f9-d3b6c8935454","timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:50:06.030Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b60a055e6d93901","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9009 decomposition"}
